    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">Feasibility Study - Port Expansion and Intermodal Rail Terminal, through Hudson-Arvon, LLC</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">The objective of the feasibility study (Study) is to increase trade flows between the Pacific Ocean and Caribbean Sea through infrastructure upgrades at existing port bottlenecks: port enhancements to improve capacity at the Port of San Lorenzo and an inland intermodal rail terminal (Intermodal Terminal) to relieve congestion and handle increased cargo at the Port of Corts. The Activity would be overseen by the Grantee, the National Interoceanic Railway Commission, and would be conducted by Hudson-Arvon, LLC, leveraging U.S. expertise in port and inland intermodal terminal development to drive U.S. exports.</narrative>
    </description>
